"commit_sha":"56e7329554398bf95b6e01ffb60b3402d64c0413","position":"1785477394397839001-2d612f4a-5fa7-4606-99db-64716a864ae9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"aeab749be5072b96624271b0857224e9a357a806283e2e44d893ce829c06cc50","event_uuid":"bade4172-c43b-4b0d-a293-4eed6d71e4b8","position":{"commit_sha":"5fce23c295a02f63855b40deb12756e31830a9a2","position":"1785477552094916199-bade4172-c43b-4b0d-a293-4eed6d71e4b8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6c018699bf261c8a77ffc030a31d261703c4f4c7248c0f41b20b9afd0aef1ac0","event_uuid":"e5a764e7-7ed9-4d4e-9b7b-69f56e7d0239","position":{"commit_sha":"0c439c778beb0025308c704a08e89e1be3790818","position":"1785478507478331001-e5a764e7-7ed9-4d4e-9b7b-69f56e7d0239"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"631b857f948930d6d3dec8b648695168191fe3bb6738957db4fc1a39d070992f","event_uuid":"c116964c-e7bb-444a-8d32-4497cdf35947","position":{"commit_sha":"aac851f32036157394e936bcfc013520c6dbd4c0","position":"1785479023226310001-c116964c-e7bb-444a-8d32-4497cdf35947"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation in progress (worktree tok-30a2). Mechanism chosen: the ModelProfile capabilities seam (change 1014 / f184) is NOT on origin/main (feature branch only) and does not expose max output tokens, so the fallback applies: a per-model max-output table (MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS) beside sizing.largest_window_tokens — haiku-4-5: 64000, sonnet-4-6: 128000, opus-4-8: 128000, unknown -> DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS (16000). Applied via passes._max_output_cfg at all six bespoke builders (pass1_chunk incl. AGENT, pass1_container, pass1_isf, summarize_for_isf, pass2_completion, pass4_coach) + the prerequisite finder per-bin call (post-ladder-escalation), and via a new 'output_budget: model_max' with-input on the workflow verify (both arms), prerequisite-verifier, and coach steps (agentic verify keeps output_tokens_per_item as an additional floor-raiser for unmapped models). Bounded-recovery output_token_limit clamps untouched. Transport check: runner passes explicit per-request timeout (cfg.timeout_s) so the Anthropic SDK's large-max_tokens streaming guard does not fire; wall-clock bound unchanged. New tests: tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_output_budget.py (16 passing); lint+typecheck+workflow suite green.","timestamp":1785478507478331001}],"created_at":1785476746455672001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4fce7de9-338a-4899-bc53-b1ebd2b10812","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"},{"link_uuid":"94d3c237-80dc-4ebf-9a57-176f93ee2db5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9e02-b0d1-0c84-439d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nPlan review LLM calls run at the flat DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS (16000, src/rebar/llm/config.py:269) with no output-budget raise anywhere in the plan-review call sites. A structured response that exceeds the ceiling raises UnretryableOutputError (src/rebar/llm/structured.py; runner.py:628-651 degrades to INDETERMINATE) — observed live on epic a492's container review: one bin over 17 children failed after 333s, and the S7-landed exhaustiveness directive (enumerate every independent defect in one run) deliberately increases per-call finding output, widening this exposure. Truncation here has only bad outcomes: a full-cost re-review or silent loss of critical findings. The completion verifier was remediated for the same family by RAISING the output token budget (completion_recovery.py raises max_tokens, :207/:222); plan review needs the comparable remediation. Operator goal: allow effectively unlimited output tokens for plan-review calls — output is naturally bounded by the model's actual findings, and unspent max_tokens costs nothing.\n\n## Approach\nOperator scope extension: the remediation covers ALL review workflows and ALL their LLM passes — plan review (Pass-1 chunks/AGENT/container/ISF/prerequisite, Pass-2 verify + novelty + completion sub-calls, Pass-4 coach, xchecks), the four-pass code review (base finder, Round-A/Round-B overlays, Pass-2 verify, Pass-4 coach — which the Gerrit review-bot inherits), the completion verifier's PRIMARY call (its recovery path already raises; the main call must get the same model-max floor), and review_ticket. scan_spec and the overlap judge are out of scope (not review gates; their outputs are small and schema-bounded). Raise every covered call's output budget to the RESOLVED MODEL'S MAXIMUM output capacity (the API requires a finite max_tokens, so model-max IS the unlimited setting). Mechanism: the runner already lets a request raise the config floor (runner.effective_max_tokens — a request may only raise, and req.output_token_limit still clamps down where bounded recovery needs it). Add a per-model max-output lookup — check first whether the just-landed ModelProfile capabilities seam (change 1014, f184: read capabilities from ModelProfile) exposes max output tokens and use it; otherwise a small table beside sizing.largest_window_tokens with a conservative fallback to the current default for unknown models. Apply it at the plan-review request builders: Pass-1 finder chunks and AGENT criteria, container bins, ISF finder/summarizer, prerequisite finder, and the verify/coach workflow steps (whichever do not already scale via output_tokens_per_item — the verify agentic arm's existing per-item scaling and 64000 ceiling may be replaced by or reconciled with model-max; state the final rule uniformly). Bounded-recovery paths that intentionally clamp via output_token_limit are untouched. Verify timeout interaction: larger max_tokens must not trip request timeouts (cfg.timeout_s; the SDK's streaming requirement for long requests is handled at the transport — confirm by reading anthropic_model.py). Alternative rejected: per-bin child-count scaling (this ticket's earlier draft) — still an arbitrary ceiling; any finite budget below model-max re-creates the truncation class the operator ruled out.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py and src/rebar/llm/plan_review/prerequisites.py (request builders), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py (or the ModelProfile seam: model max-output lookup, shared by all workflows), src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml, src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml, src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/completion-verification.yaml (step budgets reconciled to the one model-max rule), src/rebar/llm/completion.py (primary verifier call floor), src/rebar/llm/operations.py (review_ticket), code-review step builders under src/rebar/llm/code_review/ as needed, tests/unit/workflow/test_review_output_budget.py (new, covering every workflow's request fields), tests updated where they pin request max_tokens.\n\n## Testing\nUnit with a recording FakeRunner: every plan-review request carries max_tokens equal to the resolved model's max output (per the lookup) and never below DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS; unknown model falls back to the default; output_token_limit clamps still apply where set; the verify arm's budget follows the stated final rule; existing plan-review workflow tests pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every LLM request in the plan-review, code-review, and completion-verification workflows plus review_ticket carries the resolved model's maximum output budget, floor-raised through the existing runner contract (checked: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_review_output_budget.py` asserting request fields per workflow and per pass, including code-review overlays and the completion verifier's primary call).\n- [ ] Unknown/unmapped models fall back to the current default without error (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] Bounded-recovery output_token_limit clamps are unaffected (checked: existing recovery tests pass).\n- [ ] A synthetic oversized-findings container fixture that previously raised UnretryableOutputError at 16000 completes under the raised budget (checked: unit test with a FakeRunner that enforces the request ceiling).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py","reason":"raise output budget at request builders"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"model max-output lookup (or ModelProfile seam)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml","reason":"reconcile verify/coach budgets"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_output_budget.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9e02-b0d1-0c84-439d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6c7c99cb-369c-401e-8f7a-1f55b04e5870","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["gate-economics"],"ticket_id":"30a2-4f2a-dd5a-45a0","ticket_type":"bug","title":"plan-review container bins have no output-token scaling (UnretryableOutputError on large child sets)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["957f463c-c839-475c-9db9-12282a2ed620","4fce7de9-338a-4899-bc53-b1ebd2b10812","6cd0398b-93dd-4d5c-8de2-ad6cfa98eccb","ef7c2626-ab4a-4584-a62a-0454267c4afc","50156dd3-5601-47f0-8220-1fedfb2eadde","6c7c99cb-369c-401e-8f7a-1f55b04e5870","2d612f4a-5fa7-4606-99db-64716a864ae9","bade4172-c43b-4b0d-a293-4eed6d71e4b8","e5a764e7-7ed9-4d4e-9b7b-69f56e7d0239","c116964c-e7bb-444a-8d32-4497cdf35947","94d3c237-80dc-4ebf-9a57-176f93ee2db5"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785479510605685780,"uuid":"3bc84ba0-04ed-450f-b90c-3e2bc503e6d2"}